── Root Cause ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  BUILD's `workspace-service` has a specification defect in
  `blueprint/FEATURE-WORKSPACE.md:165`: `assert rows[0]["id"] == ids[1]`. The
  acceptance check appends two directories and moves the second up one position,
  but requires it to become first in the entire collection without establishing
  an empty collection. Existing rows can therefore make correct adjacent movement
  fail this assertion. The record does not establish a product implementation
  defect.

── Details ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  • `blueprint/FEATURE-WORKSPACE.md:22–23,28` specifies append behavior,
    contiguous priorities, and movement one row up or down.
  • `blueprint/FEATURE-WORKSPACE.md:142–156` creates two appended rows using
    `create_app()` without establishing an empty database or recording the
    existing order.
  • `blueprint/FEATURE-WORKSPACE.md:157–165` moves the second row up once, checks
    contiguous priorities, then incorrectly requires global first position.
  • `workspace-move.py:35`, quoted in `20260910.190108.175Z_marina_build_codex.log`,
    fails with `AssertionError` on `assert rows[0]["id"] == ids[1]`; reported
    `ids = [4, 5]` does not reveal the complete collection.
  • `20260910.190108.175Z_marina_build_codex.log:46` records the stopping message:
    `repair: stopped — deterministic acceptance score did not improve on 2 consecutive calls`.

  Not defects
  · The repair plateau at `…190108.175Z_marina_build_codex.log:45–47` is the
    consequence of the repeated acceptance failure.
  · The trusted-directory refusal in `…171121.784Z_marina_build_codex.log` was
